## Module 3: Manual Implementation of SSR & Hydration

To understand how SSR works under the hood without framework abstractions (like Next.js or Remix), let's build a server-rendered React application from scratch using **Node.js**, **Express**, and **`ReactDOMServer`**.

### 3.1 Step 1: The Server Implementation (`server.js`)

```javascript
// server.js
const express = require("express");
const path = require("path");
const React = require("react");
const ReactDOMServer = require("react-dom/server");

// Import the top-level application component
const App = require("./src/App");

const app = express();

// Serve compiled static client-side JS bundles from the /build directory
app.use("/static", express.static(path.join(__dirname, "build/static")));

// Catch-all route handler for SSR
app.get("*", (req, res) => {
  // 1. Synchronously render the component tree to an HTML string
  const componentHtml = ReactDOMServer.renderToString(<App />);

  // 2. Construct the full HTML document response
  const fullHtml = `
    <!DOCTYPE html>
    <html lang="en">
      <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8" />
        <title>Manual SSR Application</title>
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/main.css" />
      </head>
      <body>
        <!-- Inject the pre-rendered HTML into the root mount point -->
        <div id="root">${componentHtml}</div>

        <!-- Script tag pointing to the client-side hydration bundle -->
        <script src="/static/js/bundle.js"></script>
      </body>
    </html>
  `;

  // 3. Send the fully constructed HTML response
  res.setHeader("Content-Type", "text/html");
  res.send(fullHtml);
});

app.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log("SSR Server listening on http://localhost:3000");
});
```

---

### 3.2 Step 2: The Client Entry Point (`src/index.js`)

```javascript
// src/index.js
import React from "react";
import { hydrateRoot } from "react-dom/client";
import App from "./App";

// Hydrate the pre-rendered HTML generated by server.js
hydrateRoot(
  document.getElementById("root"),
  <App />
);
```

